  "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a 20-layer dielectric multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate for dual-bandpass transmission. Layer stack: CaF2 | Layer1(Ge) | Layer2(ZnS) | Layer3(Ge) | Layer4(ZnS) | Layer5(Ge) | Layer6(ZnS) | Layer7(Ge) | Layer8(ZnS) | Layer9(Ge) | Layer10(ZnS) | Layer11(Ge) | Layer12(ZnS) | Layer13(Ge) | Layer14(ZnS) | Layer15(Ge) | Layer16(ZnS) | Layer17(Ge) | Layer18(ZnS) | Layer19(Ge) | Layer20(ZnS) | Air. Optimize all 20 layer thicknesses in range 100-2000 nm. Wavelength range: 3600-5200 nm with dense sampling. Incident medium: Air at 0 degrees. Substrate: CaF2. Target: maximize transmittance in 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm bands, minimize transmittance in 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm bands. Use multi-objective optimization with weighted spectral averaging. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize the thicknesses of 20 alternating Ge and ZnS layers on a CaF2 substrate to maximize transmittance in the 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm passbands while minimizing transmittance in the 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm stopbands, within a 3600-5200 nm spectral sweep at normal incidence and unpolarized light.",
